 "path": "continual-arc-notes.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC: replicate pattern across uniform separator lines

Observed task family (examples: task-b563b005): A grid may contain one or more full rows/columns of a uniform separator color. These lines split the grid into rectangular panels. A panel contains a pattern and corresponding panels contain blanks/background; copy the pattern into each corresponding panel while preserving separator lines and all existing pattern cells. Use the demos to identify which panel provides the source; it may be a corner or another panel. The non-separator cells considered blank/background in the demos were 0 or the dominant panel background color.

Evidence: In 14x13 demo, full 6-colored row/column lines divide 4x6 panels; the populated bottom-left panel was copied to all four panel positions. In 9x13 demo, 9-colored lines divide four panels; populated top-right pattern was replicated into all panels. Test 5x3 had full row [8,8,8] dividing two panels, with the lower panel's 2x3 pattern [[7,7,5],[5,4,5]] copied into the upper panel, leaving the separator row intact. Validate panel dimensions, separator placement, and exact copying before submission."
